{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/780528-werewolves-with-multiple-moon-gifts","id":780528,"title":"Werewolves with multiple Moon Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-05T06:28:32-08:00","id":780528,"title":"Werewolves with multiple Moon Gifts","content":"To jump right in here is my issue, as we all know Werewolves have one Auspice given to them by Luna during their First Change. As such they get their first Moon Gifts and Shadow Gifts. I was reading over and refreshing my knowledge on the gaining of new Gifts and I came across some wording I don\u2019t quite understand because it almost sounds like a Rahu could get Cahalith Gifts. Please calm yourselves I can already hear the growling I don\u2019t think this is what it means but let me lay it out for you now, I will site page numbers I am using a PDF so forgive me if it\u2019s off a page or so.<br /> <br /> So the gaining of Gifts and Facets is covered on Pg#114, the first bit we all know and makes sense. During First Change a werewolf gets his first gift, he unlocks gifts as his Renown increases and so on. But then there is this (See evidence A), which says a Werewolf can discover new Moon Gifts that are associated with their Auspice. It even goes on to talk about them buying the dotes in order, and that these new Moon Gifts cannot be higher than their Auspice Renown.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are associated with her auspice at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift. Gaining further Facets costs 2 Experiences each, and they must be purchased in ascending order. An Uratha can never raise the dots in a Moon Gift above the rating of her current auspice Renown.</li> </ol>My First thought was this was talking about affinity Gift lists, but that is covered on the next page Pg#115. Which states (See evidence B) a separate experience cost for favored Gift list and mentions both Tribe and Auspice.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Unlocking a Shadow Gift costs 5 Experiences, or 3 if itis favored by auspice or tribe.</li> </ol>So to wrap up this drawn out post with I apologies for, what do you all think it means is this like in the old Lore of the Forsaken book where we got the Warrior Moon, and the Witch Moon lists. An as of right now there are no alternative Moon lists released. Or does it mean that Any Werewolf can get Gifts that belong to other Moons just slower. The base character sheet even has two places to right down Moon gifts as if to track two separate lists. I am not taking sides on this fight right now I merely laying this down before the forum to see what people think and to see if others have had this question.<br /> Thank you very much for your time, and Happy Hunting <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10059-ak_cahalith","name":"AK_Cahalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:34:02-08:00","id":780533,"title":"","content":"That line is put there to allow for future material to work, like a 2nd edition version of those Lore of the Forsaken Auspice Gifts (Warrior Moon, Judge Moon and so on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:41:47-08:00","id":780536,"title":"","content":"Hopefully the next book will come out soon so people will have other auspices and understand. It's a common query.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T06:46:28-08:00","id":780538,"title":"","content":"I kind of assumed that is what it ment, becuse I would not be a fan of letting players get multiple Auspice lists lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10059-ak_cahalith","name":"AK_Cahalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:12:39-08:00","id":780630,"title":"","content":"I always interpret it, as open for the ST to determine if auspice gifts can be gotten by other auspice or not.<br /> <br /> While mechanically it would be a nightmare of balancing (level 1 rahu gift + level 1 irraka gift) setting wise it kinda made sense, if you look at the renown table on the book it list that for a werewolf to reach rank 3+ he has to get other renowns aside from his own.<br /> <br /> In WtA a elder garou was a master of his own auspice and his role in garou society but on Forsaken, the &quot;ideal&quot; elder is like father wolf an apex predator master of all the hunt.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T11:37:10-08:00","id":780639,"title":"","content":"&quot;A werewolf may discover other Moon Gifts that are <b>associated with her auspice</b> at a cost of 5 Experiences, which unlocks the first dot Facet of the Gift.&quot;<br /> <br /> The bolded section is key in determining that it is not and will never be (probably) the intent for Uratha to get the Moon Gifts associated other auspices. To corroborate that, before every Moon Gift is a disclaimer that makes it clear. It's easy to miss, but &quot;This Gift is only available to Ithaeur&quot; appears before The Crescent Moon Gift, for example. <br /> <br /> Though I like the idea of an apex Uratha who has mastered all Moons, I don't think it will ever happen without some sort of incredibly powerful, borderline blasphemous rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-05T14:25:43-08:00","id":780707,"title":"","content":"Indeed, you absolutely cannot learn auspice gifts associated with another auspice, only your own. The intention is for there to be more than one gift associated with a given auspice at some point in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T07:21:19-08:00","id":781123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/780528-werewolves-with-multiple-moon-gifts?p=780707#post780707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, you absolutely cannot learn auspice gifts associated with another auspice, only your own. The intention is for there to be more than one gift associated with a given auspice at some point in the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if one has been transformed by an Idigam, and been granted their ability to steal Gifts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T07:34:46-08:00","id":781129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/780528-werewolves-with-multiple-moon-gifts?p=781123#post781123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if one has been transformed by an Idigam, and been granted their ability to steal Gifts? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thaaaaaats a little bit different <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T07:47:11-08:00","id":781133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/780528-werewolves-with-multiple-moon-gifts?p=781129#post781129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thaaaaaats a little bit different <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, would it be possible for an Idigam to grant that power to a Herald, or suchlike?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T10:26:08-08:00","id":781193,"title":"","content":"It seems like the auspice is chosen by Luna herself, not a lune. So they might not be able to give you a new auspice the normal way, but with their ability to taint essence maybe they could sculpt a reasonable facsimile or since they can swap souls they can probably shove the soul of a werewolf with another auspice into you which might do something similar.<br /> <br /> Alternatively they might be able to get you the gifts with an ability similar to flayed lunes. Or they could just shove a lune in your soul. On the off-chance that Luna makes you auspice'd by putting a lune into the spirit-side of your soul it should be something an idigam could replicate.<br /> <br /> Probably the type of thing that's up to a ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-06-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T17:21:07-08:00","id":781407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/780528-werewolves-with-multiple-moon-gifts?p=781133#post781133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that note, would it be possible for an Idigam to grant that power to a Herald, or suchlike?</div> </div> </div> </div> No; an idigam can imprint a copy of a Dread Power or numina on a Herald, but not an Essence Shaping ability, and Thief of Gifts is an Essence Shaping power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}